# xc2/tests/deck.nxs - drive XC2 through the prologue and capture shots, deterministically.
#
# Run (from xc2\build\boot, so game/romfs is next to the exe):
#   $env:NXRT_TEST_SCRIPT='...\xc2\tests\deck.nxs'
#   $env:NXRT_TEST_OUT='testout_deck'; $env:NXRT_TEST_DETERMINISTIC='1'; $env:NXRT_TEST_FRAME_SOURCE='tick'
#   .\xc2_boot.exe --exefs <fefw-recomp>\work\xc2ns2 --link host --gfx window --log deck_tt.log
#
# Why: the prologue's scenes run on the GAME clock, so with @rate 30
@timeout 20000          # every later wait may take this many frames (default 3600 is under the opening's length) (one frame = exactly 1/30 s of game time) a scene lands on
# a fixed FRAME number instead of a wall-clock time that drifts between runs (HANDOVER 21.8). @shot writes
# <out>/shots/<name>.png at that frame and does not block.
#
# XC2 has no game probes (they are Metroid Prime only), so no @warp/@area: the opening is walked with pad presses and frame
# waits. Loading runs on the host clock, hence @sleep.

@rate 30
@timeout 20000          # every later wait may take this many frames (default 3600 is under the opening's length)
@log deck.nxs: boot + title presses
600
press A
60
press A
60
press A
@sleep 3000

# A sweep: the ship deck (dragon + Rex) is somewhere in the middle; the shots name their frame so the next script can cut
# straight to it.
@frame 1800
@shot 1800
@frame 2200
@shot 2200
@frame 2600
@shot 2600
@frame 3000
@shot 3000
@frame 3400
@shot 3400
@frame 3800
@shot 3800
@frame 4200
@shot 4200
@frame 4600
@shot 4600
@frame 5000
@shot 5000
@frame 5400
@shot 5400
@frame 5800
@shot 5800
@frame 6200
@shot 6200
@frame 6600
@shot 6600
@frame 7000
@shot 7000

@pass
